cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LOXDockAudit, please cite the software using this metadata."
type: software
title: "LOXDockAudit: Control-aware productive-geometry analysis for LOX-collagen docking screens"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-05-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/G1F12/LOXDockAudit"
url: "https://github.com/G1F12/LOXDockAudit"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20241797"
abstract: >
  LOXDockAudit is a computational docking-analysis and reproducibility
  framework for LOX-collagen screens. It evaluates whether docked poses satisfy
  active-site distance and optional substrate-orientation geometry criteria,
  supports control-aware comparisons including catalytically inactive controls,
  performs structural quality checks, and generates auditable CSV, Markdown,
  and SVG reports. The software is intended for computational interpretation of
  docking poses and does not provide experimental validation of enzymatic
  activity or biological efficacy.
keywords:
  - lysyl oxidase
  - collagen
  - docking
  - structural biology
  - bioinformatics
  - computational biology
  - reproducibility
  - protein engineering
